306	 * One (1,2)-swap pass in the sense of Andrade/Resende/Werneck (2012).
307	 *
308	 * A vertex v outside the set with exactly one neighbour u inside it is a swap
309	 * centre: removing u frees v and every other neighbour of u that was blocked
310	 * only by u, and re-adding two of those neighbours grows the set by one.
311	 * Each vertex participates in at most one swap per pass.  Returns the net
312	 * change in set size (never negative).
313	 */
